  "mash_knn_training_cv": {
    "note": "REVISED 2026-09-08: an earlier version of this docstring flagged this as circular (phylogroups derived from Mash distances scoring a Mash-distance classifier). That concern doesn't hold: phylogroups are built by WITHIN-species clustering (Methods \u00a74) over genomes already assigned to species by NCBI taxonomy, so the CV grouping has no mechanism to inflate SPECIES-level separation, which is what this classifier is scored on. The all-k tie at exactly 1.000 reflects the real, expected geometry: inter-species Mash distance dwarfs intra-species distance for six organisms spanning two phyla. Mash/ANI-based whole-genome relatedness is the modern standard for bacterial species delineation (operationalised in GTDB) and is treated as the PRIMARY R1-4 comparator, not a sanity check.",
